course: dictionary
lesson: 13855
title: Joyfully: showing how it feels
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Joyfully tells you how someone does something. It means in a very happy, glad way, full of joy. Look for the action word first, then ask: how did they do it? That is where joyfully lives.
explain: «The children ran joyfully into the garden.» The action is ran. Joyfully tells us how they ran: happily, and full of joy, not just running to get somewhere.
explain: Stories and songs use it a lot. «The choir sang joyfully at Christmas.» Joyfully shows the feeling is strong and happy, more than «happily» does.
fact: Joyfully is an adverb, so it tells us how someone does an action.
fact: «Joyfully» means in a very happy, glad way, full of joy.
fact: The root word is joy, a very strong feeling of happiness.
fact: «Joyfully» shows a stronger feeling than «happily».
fact: A good check is to ask: how did they do it? If the answer is with great happiness, joyfully fits.
exercise: «The puppy wagged its tail joyfully when we came home.» What does joyfully mean here? | In a quiet, hidden way | *In a very happy, glad way | In a sleepy, slow way | In a cross, angry way
exercise: Copy the word that tells how she sang: «She sang joyfully at the party.» | at | party | *joyfully | she
exercise: Jayden says joyfully just means happily. Why is that not quite right? | It is just a longer word | They mean exactly the same, so there is no difference at all | *Joyfully shows a stronger, fuller joy | Joyfully means sad
test: «The dog barked joyfully when its owner came home.» What does joyfully tell us? | *How the dog barked: in a happy, glad way | Where the dog barked | The name of the dog | When the dog was born
test: Which word means in a very happy, glad way? | *joyfully | sadly | carefully | quietly
exam: Ben writes, «The sun rose joyfully over the hills.» Does joyfully tell us how the sun rose, or when it rose? | *How the sun rose, in a glad way | Who saw the sun rise | Which hill the sun rose over | When the sun rose, at dawn
